        "body": "I finished my review and found nothing to comment on. Nice work! :tada:\n\n- Reconciled my earlier thread: the fake `NotFoundError` is gone and `GetWithSource` now guards the local read with `skipLocal`, so that point is fixed.\n- Checked the new read path. For glab-managed keys it goes straight to the global lookup. Other keys keep their local-over-global behavior.\n- Checked `IsGlobalOnlyKey`. It resolves aliases through `ConfigKeyEquivalence`, and the set is built from `KeySchema` at init, so aliases and names are both covered.\n- Checked `config set`. A glab-managed key routes both the set and the write to the global config, with and without `--global`, and the hostname path is unchanged.\n- Checked the tests. They cover both halves of the fix, the schema drift guard and local precedence for ordinary keys. I found no problems."
      },
